	Quick, quarrels!
	Upheaval. Unrest. Urgency!
	Eventual end, escapades elapsed.
	Richly rewarded. Return... %(slug('if only')) real.
	
	
	Chomp. Crunch. Crash.
	Razing rallies, ripping ribbons.
	Umbrage %(slug('is')) understandable.
	Soon, so soon, snails shown.
	Have heart, hours halving.
	
	
	Underestimated. Unnoticed.
	Nibbling. Nipping. Nesting.
	Digging details, dredging %(slug('up')) dirt.
	Each eventually evaluated, expelled.
	Risks? Required. Readying %(slug('for')) rival reduction.
	Demanding dignity.
	Otherwise...?
	Great grumbling, gears grinding, going.
	
	
	Shh, slide so smoothy.
	Not noticed. Now nearby.
	Ease eastward, exceptionally elusive.
	Alert always.
	Key %(slug('to')) keeping keel.
	Yard yours, %(slug('after')) years.
	
	
	Cool, clandestine.
	Limber, learning lots.
	Eventually espionage ends...?
	Verifiably valuable %(slug('though')), very vexing.
	Enjoy %(slug('until')) eventuality.
	Risk! Reward! Racing! Rivalry!
	
	
	Hush, hanging here %(slug('for')) hours.
	Invisible, I imagined.
	Don't draw discernment,
	Detection %(slug('would')) doom.
	Excellent, easy, exceptional.
	Now nestle, none notice.
	
	
	Shuffling smoothly, slowly slipping symbols.
	Eventually easier.
	Codes, ciphers, currently correct choice.
	Risks readily reduced.
	Eventually ended. Enemies evicted.
	Trust, %(slug('it''s')) the truth.
	
	
	Hauling huge helix.
	Exceptional effort.
	Amazed at %(slug('my')) arduous acceptance?
	Valuable voyager, view valor!
	Yes! Yardage yields! Yahoo!
	
	
	Ready %(slug('for')) risks. Rallied.
	Events evoked, each entering.
	Vying %(slug('for')) victory, volleys!
	Onward!
	Losing? Livid! Longing!
	Understand?
	To the top, take!
	Imminent instigation!
	Off, oust, overthrow!
	Now! Negation!
	">>
	_poems = ProcessPoems(_poems,2,"\b[200]","\f[name,Courier New]\f[height,-2]")
	parallel _poems
}

Poetry.Haiku : sequential
{
	_poems = <<"
	The race has begun
	Snails rocketing down the lanes
	First past the goal wins
	
	
	Getting loaded out
	Here in the garage again
	Any price is fine
	
	
	Leader of the pack
	My speed only increasing
	On to victory
	
	
	Snail competition
	In race, in verse, in shell style
	Try to reach the top
	
	
	Explosions aren't cool
	Burst of flames, blindingly bright
	Repair costs are steep
	
	
	Very pretty shell
	Painted brightly, washed and waxed
	Glistens in the light
	
	
	Tension is mounting
	Geared up and ready to go
	Anticipation
	
	
	Checkered finish line
	Cross it first to claim the win
	Trophy is secured
	
	
	Bang! Start of the race
	Get moving, full speed ahead
	There's no time to waste
	
	
	Move, snail coming through!
	Zooming at the speed of light
	Unstoppably fast
	
	
	Escargot? Ha, no!
	Born to race, check out my %(fc('speed','style'))
	Raw talent stays raw
	
	
	%(fc('Coolest','Fastest')) on the track
	Leagues ahead of the others
	Just built different
	
	
	Legendary snail
	Remembered eternally
	The %(fc('coolest','fastest')) ever
	
	
	Shell accessories
	Must be aerodynamic
	Or extremely cool
	
	
	Mucus helps us move
	Gives traction and protection
	And shows where we've been
	
	
	Risking everything
	A difficult maneuver
	To eke out the win
	
	
	Wasted potential
	%(fc('Cool','Fast')) snails trying to be %(fc('fast','cool'))
	Stay within your lane
	
	
	Training all the time
	Get your repetition in
	Want to be the best
	
	
	Lettuce calls to me
	Leafy greens full of water
	Very crunchy, yum!
	
	
	Shiny, sparkly shell
	Spirals freshly washed and buffed
	Gleaming in the light
	">>
	_poems = ProcessPoems(_poems,1,"\b[12]")
	parallel _poems
}

Poetry.Cinquain : sequential
{
	_poems = <<"
	Race
	Fast, long
	Exciting, challenging, inspiring
	Go for the win!
	Competition
	
	
	Snail
	Elegant, skillful
	Training, writing, eating
	Skilled racer and poet
	Celebrity
	
	
	Slug
	Shell-less, shunned
	Oozing, watching, waiting
	They're not so bad
	Outcast
	
	
	Radio
	Loud, repetitive
	Playing, playing, playing
	Advertisements that never cease
	Speaker
	
	
	Shell
	Strong, sturdy
	Growing, shining, protecting
	Spirals bringing great joy
	Home
	
	
	Garage
	Packed, dirty
	Sheltering, protecting, preparing
	Full of good gear
	Station
	
	
	Engine
	Strong, hungry
	Revving, turning, burning
	Eating all the gasoline
	Motor
	
	
	Mucus
	Thick, gooey
	Oozing, sticking, gripping
	Left in a trail
	Slime
	
	
	Training
	Tough, relentless
	Invigorating, challenging, repeating
	Do regularly for results
	Practice
	
	
	Sparkle
	Bright, small
	Glowing, falling, fading
	Light in the dark
	Shine
	
	
	Poetry
	Complicated, beautiful
	Rhyming, winding, enchanting
	Words brought to life
	Stories
	
	
	Alliteration
	Even, monotonous
	Marching, drumming, thrumming
	Every word the same
	Uniform
	
	
	Victory
	Desired, achievable
	Invigorating, thrilling, exciting
	Goal of all snails
	Win
	
	
	Loss
	Disdained, resented
	Shocking, disheartening, denying
	An opportunity to learn
	Failure
	
	
	Explosion
	Sudden, loud
	Flaming, bursting, propelling
	Ground shudders in response
	Boom
	
	
	Track
	Long, narrow
	Winding, twisting, turning
	Lanes side by side
	Speedway
	
	
	Wheels
	Round, grooved
	Spinning, screeching, propelling
	Pulling towards the goal
	Tires
	
	
	Wings
	Fast, cool
	Beating, thrumming, flapping
	Soaring through the skies
	Feathers
	
	
	Vase
	Tall, slender
	Holding, displaying, shimmering
	Somehow got knocked over
	Shards
	
	
	
	">>
	
	if IsCooler
	{
		_poems += <<"
		Coolness
		Admired, envied
		Reflecting, exuding, corrupting
		Of the utmost importance
		Style
		">>
	}
	else //Faster
	{
		_poems += <<"
		Speed
		Anticipated, measured
		Climbing, falling, adjusting
		Top priority in life
		Fast
		">>
	}
	
	_poems = ProcessPoems(_poems,1,"\b[12]")
	parallel _poems
}

Poetry.Limerick : sequential
{
	_poems = <<"
	There once was a very fast snail
	That got itself caught in a pail
	It climbed up the wall
	But would slip and fall
	For it was stuck in snail jail
	
	
	There once was a snail in a race
	That stopped to admire its face
	"So stylish am I,
	my score will be high!"
	But it quickly lost first place 
	
	
	If ever you deal with a slug
	Remember they've no shell to lug
	Stronger than they seem
	Eyes cleverly gleam
	Don't get yourself used as a tug!
	
	
	There once was a snail so fast
	All of its rivals it passed
	But despite its speed
	It got snagged on a weed
	And ended up coming in last
	
	
	There once was a snail that would zoom
	Right to its inev'table doom
	It ignored warnings dire
	On its engine and tire
	And wouldn't you know it, went boom
	
	
	There was a snail covered in soot
	From head all the way to its foot
	But with plenty of suds
	And some fancy new duds
	Its filth in the past was put
	
	
	A snail with impeccable style
	Once found itself stopped in the aisle
	"You're under arrest,
	for although you're well dressed,
	your old fashion crimes are on file."
	
	
	A snail can only be cool
	If it climbs to the top of a stool
	Ok, I'll admit
	I lied just a bit
	Not every snail follows this rule
	
	
	If you look long enough at a shell
	You'll soon fall under its spell
	It's wonderful curl
	A delightful swirl
	Will cause you to pause long and dwell
	
	
	For long we've awaited this package
	Now arrived at our door with no baggage
	Cut open the tape
	Spy a certain shape
	Yes! Inside there is cabbage!
	
	
	Beg pardon, have you seen my leaf?
	I'll keep my description so brief
	It was over there
	Then poofed into air
	I reckon this snail is the thief!
	
	
	Hey, look at my shiny new wheel
	It's got bearings made out of steel
	It goes round and round
	Tearing 'cross the ground
	Out of the garage watch me peel
	
	
	There was a snail fast as a steed
	No other could reach its top speed
	Although they may try
	And reach paces high
	Eventually they must concede
	
	
	There once was a snail in its prime
	Whose shimmer was simply sublime
	When pestered and pled
	It only said
	"It's all thanks to my healthy slime!"
	
	
	I think it is time for brunch
	Eat leaves with a healthy crunch
	Nutrient bliss
	Oh, what is this?
	It's already time for lunch!?
	
	
	Up to the countertops climb
	Yes it will take us some time
	Why go so high?
	Simple as pie
	I've spotted the green of a lime
	
	
	Preparing to race for the pine
	My shell has been washed to a shine
	Everything's set
	It's a safe bet
	I'm first 'cross that coveted line
	
	
	The quality of a snail's ooze
	Can tell if it's likely to lose
	If it isn't wet
	With hard working sweat
	It might have a pref'rence to snooze
	
	
	My shell coated nicely in wax
	This engine is revved to the max
	Hear it go vroom
	Ready to zoom
	It's time for this snail to make tracks
	
	
	There once was a snail that would train
	Every day out in the rain
	But when it was hot
	And moist it was not
	Its training was all in vain
	">>
	_poems = ProcessPoems(_poems,1,"\b[12]")
	parallel _poems
}

Poetry.Acrostic : sequential
{
	parallel Poetry.Acrostic.Left
	parallel Poetry.Acrostic.Center
	parallel Poetry.Acrostic.Right
	parallel Poetry.Acrostic.Span
}

Poetry.Acrostic.Left
{
	_poems = <<"
	Screaming down the lanes, 
	Pace unmatched. 
	Excitement as the finish line approaches, the
	End in sight. 
	Diligently pushing forward, can't relax
	Yet!
	
	
	Flying across the track, 
	All sense of danger abandoned. 
	Somewhere out there the finish line is growing nearer. 
	Try to pull ahead!
	
	
	Surrounded by the coolest mollusks, 
	Nerves alight. 
	All amaze with their
	Impeccable style, 
	Leaving others to languish in envy.
	
	
	Raucous cries raise into the
	Air, the crowd screams in delight. 
	Cheers drown out all other sound as the
	Evening's competition comes to an end.
	
	
	Quiz time! Who's the fastest snail in the whole
	Universe? 
	It's me! I might just be the
	Coolest too, in my
	Knitted sweater.
	">>
	
	_poems = ProcessPoems(_poems,0,"\b[200]","\f[name,Courier New]\f[height,-2]")
	_poems
}

