Poetry.Lyric : sequential
{
	_poems = <<"
	%(note1)Oh, don't you wanna cross that finish line?%(note2)
	%(note1)Oh, don't you wanna have the fastest time?%(note2)
	
	
	%(note1)Just between%(note2)
	%(note1)you and me%(note2)
	%(note1)I'd eat the leaves%(note2)
	%(note1)right off that tree%(note2)
	
	
	%(note1)Hey, hey, don't forget to check your rearview mirror%(note2)
	%(note1)Objects in it may be much nearer%(note2)
	
	
	%(note1)Whoosh! Feel the shockwave when I zoom by%(note2)
	%(note1)Catch up to me? Please, I'd love to see you try%(note2)
	
	
	%(note1)Wheels on fire, burning rubber%(note2)
	%(note1)Need for speed, feel it shudder%(note2)
	
	
	%(note1)And as the fire shoots past my shell, paint licked by flames%(note2)
	%(note1)I find myself asking "why are snails trying to fly? We arent planes!"%(note2)
	
	
	%(note1)Oh, I'm sorry that I let you down%(note2)
	%(note1)My best wasn't good enough%(note2)
	%(note1)Oh, don't leave me here alone%(note2)
	%(note1)Coming in second place is rough%(note2)
	
	
	%(note1)Oh, show me that spiral shell%(note2)
	%(note1)How'd you grow it curved so well?%(note2)
	%(note1)Share your secret with me, I won't tell%(note2)
	%(note1)I'd love a place like that to dwell%(note2)
	
	
	%(note1)Training, training, every day%(note2)
	%(note1)They'll give you classes if you pay%(note2)
	%(note1)Muscles growing all the way%(note2)
	%(note1)You can't keep this snail at bay%(note2)
	
	
	%(note1)Oh, you're always there for me%(note2)
	%(note1)In your hold I'd never fear%(note2)
	%(note1)Strong and smooth, keeping me safe%(note2)
	%(note1)Mucus, I'm so glad you're here!%(note2)
	
	
	%(note1)Gotta go, gotta zoom, outta my way, make room!%(note2)
	%(note1)Got places to be, like up that tree, there's no stopping me!%(note2)
	
	
	%(note1)Hey%(note2)
	%(note1)I know you said it's over%(note2)
	%(note1)But I just have one request%(note2)
	%(note1)Please%(note2)
	%(note1)Just tell me you'll think it over%(note2)
	%(note1)Look at the race scores and reassess!%(note2)
	
	
	%(note1)Oh, sweet leaf of green%(note2)
	%(note1)Life bringer%(note2)
	%(note1)My dinner%(note2)
	%(note1)Lettuce, you're as lovely as a queen!%(note2)
	
	
	%(note1)Hey hey hey, don't let those old leaves get you down%(note2)
	%(note1)There's plenty of fresh lettuce still to go around%(note2)
	
	
	%(note1)It's remarkable, reliable and strong%(note2)
	%(note1)The way it waves, pulling you along%(note2)
	%(note1)Covered in mucus, and here with you lifelong!%(note2)
	%(note1)Trust your foot, it'll never steer you wrong%(note2)
	
	
	%(note1)Oh, those great snails of old%(note2)
	%(note1)Daring, immaculate, and bold%(note2)
	%(note1)One day I hope I'll be a legend too%(note2)
	%(note1)And that I might somehow inspire you!%(note2)
	
	
	%(note1)High scores aren't the only thing in life, it's true%(note2)
	%(note1)But they sure are fun, so I hope you'll try for them too%(note2)
	
	
	%(note1)Exploring the cabinets under cover of night%(note2)
	%(note1)No one to stop me, I find some lettuce and stop for a bite%(note2)
	%(note1)At that moment, I hear a click, the room goes bright...!%(note2)
	%(note1)Ah! I've been caught! Plucked from the cupboard, into the light%(note2)
	
	
	%(note1)Oozing along, having a good time%(note2)
	%(note1)Off to the store, to get me some key lime%(note2)
	%(note1)Very hungry, it's getting near lunchtime%(note2)
	%(note1)Got no money, time for some lunch crime!%(note2)
	
	
	%(note1)Out here on the track, we're racing to win%(note2)
	%(note1)Got no time to slack, we're going all in%(note2)
	">>
	_poems = ProcessPoems(_poems,1,"\b[12]")
	parallel _poems
}

note
{
	"\f[name,arial]♪\f[name,default]"
	"\f[name,arial]♫\f[name,default]"
}

Poetry.Rhyming_Couplet : sequential
{
	_poems = <<"
	The race has ended
	Victor decided
	Trophy presented
	Accolades spendid
	
	
	The finish line crossed, the crowd roars
	A new record set, highest scores
	
	
	Time spent in the garage
	Is like a nice massage
	An outfitting montage
	Will improve our barrage
	
	
	It's time for a trial
	To see if you have style
	Ah, reason to smile
	Your coolness is on file
	
	
	Leafy lanes, the place to be
	Under canopy of tree
	Twisting roads fill you with glee
	Never have I felt so free
	
	
	Twists and turns confound
	Climbing up this mound
	Up this trail we've wound
	High up off the ground
	
	
	Fresh new coat of paint
	Rivals feeling faint
	Show them no restraint
	With victory acquaint=
	
	
	Slowly oozing 'cross the porch
	Someone left a bowl of borstch
	T'would be a shame not to consume
	This lovely meal of sweet legume~!
	
	
	Engines roar, flames lick the air
	Try and race me if you dare
	I'll beat you both in speed and flair
	Come, let's do this fair and square
	
	
	Veering to and fro
	Don't mess up my flow
	Dodging side to side
	To the finish, slide!
	
	
	Around and around the track
	Making laps, pick up the slack
	Straight ahead, stay in the lane
	Don't let rivals start to gain
	
	
	Decked out with stickers aplenty
	Upon this shell I've got twenty
	Stack them high until they tower
	Decorations raise horsepower
	
	
	Higher and higher, the ranks climb
	True greatness is built over time
	Show them your style and grace sublime
	Make your mark while still in your prime
	
	
	Sun is up, time for snacks
	To the fridge, let's make tracks
	Soon we'll come back with stacks
	Just wait here and relax
	
	
	See our snail power
	Don't hide, don't cower
	This our finest hour
	All coated in flour
	
	
	Races eternal
	Tracked in a journal
	Victors' names penned
	To later upend
	Fierce competition
	We're on a mission
	No special treatment
	Crowning achievement
	
	
	Slow and steady wins the race
	Bold lie told right to your face
	Races are won with fast pace
	Take the lead, become the ace
	
	
	Listen to the old adage
	'Make sure to eat your cabbage'
	Leaves filled with vital masses
	Of nutrients and acids
	
	
	Diets should be colorful
	Carrots, onions, wonderful
	Plums, tomatoes, all are good
	Cabbage, apples, yes you should
	Nutrients in many forms
	Yummy, eat them up in swarms
	
	
	Watch the worms go by
	Never asking why
	Simply on the move
	Got nothing to prove
	">>
	_poems = ProcessPoems(_poems,1,"\b[12]")
	parallel _poems
}

Poetry.Alternate_Rhyme : sequential
{
	_poems = <<"
	Oh to chew on lettuce green
	And feel the gentle fronds
	Get as much as you can glean
	And you'll strengthen our bonds
	
	
	Raindrops pouring down
	A gentle pitter-patter
	Be sure not to drown
	In puddles that are scatter'd
	
	
	Straight on down the lanes
	Snails do swiftly fly
	Tearing 'cross the planes
	Sparkle in their eye
	
	
	A spiral shell so shiny
	Catches every eye
	The others are so whiny
	Wishing they could buy
	
	
	Let's begin the race
	Off the starting line
	Gone without a trace
	See you at the pine
	
	
	Observe my shell
	Admire my stripes
	Isn't it swell,
	The many types?
	
	
	Inching towards the finish
	One goal on my mind
	Reaching for the spinach
	Those leaves will be mine
	
	
	Here our stories are enshrined
	Tales of old passed down
	Many fates, all intertwined
	Those who claimed the crown
	
	
	Snails so fast you can't compare
	Even if you dash
	Try and race us if you dare
	We're gone in a flash
	
	
	Never stop training
	If you want to be the best
	Even when raining
	Keep it up to beat the rest
	
	
	Opened the floodgate
	Here they come, a squirming swarm
	Watch the worms migrate
	Chasing down the latest storm
	
	
	Getting loaded out
	Mechanic adding gear
	Never any doubt
	I'll be one to fear
	
	
	Shell decorations complete
	Covered in stickers
	To show off or be discreet?
	Everyone bickers
	
	
	Freshly painted lines
	A racetrack still pristine
	Give it a few times
	No chance it will stay clean
	
	
	Starting soon, place your bets
	Snails lined up, prepared
	Track as good as it gets
	Winner to be declared
	
	
	Fancy new engine
	Twenty gears turning in time
	Listen to them spin
	Hear the roar, a sound sublime
	Now we're sure to win
	The leaderboards we will climb
	Ready for action
	Upgrades have me feeling prime
	
	
	Down the lanes, quickly zooming
	One goal in my mind
	Ignoring others booming
	Finish line I'll find
	
	
	Up and at 'em, time to train
	Practice all day long
	Work your muscles and your brain
	Snails are very strong
	
	
	Waiting for the rain
	Droplets rushing down
	Soothing for the brain
	Blanketing the town
	
	
	Climbing up the ranks so high
	Going for the crown
	Shooting off into the sky
	Try not to look down
	">>
	_poems = ProcessPoems(_poems,2,"\b[12]")
	parallel _poems
}

Poetry.Free_Verse : sequential
{
	_poems = <<"
	There is nothing like
	the crisp, 
	the crunch, 
	the cool misting
	from produce sprinklers. 
	Nibble\w8
	Nibble\w8
	Nibble\w8
	It's lettuce time.
	
	
	Engines revved. 
	Pavement slick. 
	Risking it all on the track
	Over pebbles
	Around leaves
	Faster, faster, faster
	CRACK! 
	BOOM! 
	Four snail pileup.
	
	
	Is there anything else to life
	than the pressure, building and building
	every race
	every interview
	every day spent training
	round and round the track? 
	Something, anything, more than
	work
	and toil? 
	A fresh wash, 
	new paint, 
	slick new sunglasses mark
	rebirth! 
	Who needs speed when you can be
	Cool 😎
	
	
	Back in the garage again. 
	A buzz\w8
	A whirr\w8
	A clank\w8
	The sounds of tinkering, 
	giving every snail a thrill
	at the thought
	of shiny
	new
	upgrades.
	
	
	Have you ever given thought
	to the shape
	of the track? 
	Around and around it goes, 
	never stopping
	a race unending. 
	But more than that, 
	does it remind you of something else? 
	Around and around, endlessly mesmerizing. 
	It bears a certain resemblance
	to a snail's
	spiral shell.
	
	
	The quest for food
	is never-ending. 
	A bite here
	A nibble there
	Every leaf you can find. 
	There is but one thing
	that could end our searching
	for good. 
	One singular dungeon to conquer
	to have food aplenty
	forever. 
	One great monolith
	with walls that appear impenetrable. 
	The refrigerator.
	
	
	There comes a time
	in every snail's life
	when it must decide between
	integrity
	and endorsing products
	for personal gain. 
	To stick to principles, 
	or to succumb to the pull
	of lettuce
	and shiny new gear. 
	.\w8.\w8. 
	I'll take the money, thanks.
	
	\f[italic,1]This poem brought to you by %(snailbrand[0]).\f[italic,default]
	
	
	Drip\w8
	Drip\w8
	Drip\w8
	The soft pattering
	of rain
	brings a simple joy
	to all snails. 
	Nature's cleansing, 
	washed and feeling
	fresh. 
	Moisture abundant, overflowing. 
	What more could a little snail
	ask for?
	
	
	Lettuce is often
	held in high regard. 
	But truly, any leafy green
	will do. 
	Cabbage\w8
	Spinach\w8
	Arugula\w8
	Kale\w8
	It's all delicious
	Nutritious
	And will fill your snail
	with glee. 
	\_w[2000](and leaves.)
	
	
	The sky
	is a far off dream. 
	A wide open space, 
	no obstacles
	no barriers
	just the heavens before you
	littered with clouds. 
	Tragically, the sky is fiercely claimed
	and protected
	by birds.
	
	
	To live life without
	a shell. 
	Can you imagine it? 
	No protection
	No home
	Nowhere to put stickers
	It seems unfathomably sad. 
	Perhaps one could say
	that slugs
	are the bravest of us all.
	
	
	Race day. 
	The thrill of the track. 
	Anticipation mounting, 
	the crowd roars as the signal
	is given. 
	Off the starting line, into the fray, 
	seeking an early lead. 
	Tight corners
	perfectly timed gear changes
	a bit of flair
	My training comes back to me
	in my finest hour.
	
	
	A snail without style
	is like a wing without feathers. 
	Strange
	Bare
	Never able to reach its true
	potential. 
	To forsake style is to doom
	one's racing career.
	
	
	The deciding moment. 
	Tests and trials passed, 
	all that remains is to be
	Named. 
	A racer name. 
	The unique identity upon which
	fame and fortune
	may be hung. 
	A roll of the dice, 
	so many names that they are chosen
	by chance
	out of your control. 
	Your name is... 
	.\w8.\w8. 
	\_w[2000]Not alliterative.
	
	
	Turn the dial, 
	Rotate through news
	Weather
	Music
	And more. 
	Fields of static, incomprehensible, 
	overwhelming. 
	Between them, spaces of clarity, a noise so
	wonderful
	and invigorating
	It brings a snail to life. 
	A delicate balance between chaos and harmony.
	
	
	Scrub\w8
	Scrub\w8
	Scrub\w8
	Foamy suds building up
	Water warm, sponge squishy
	Soon will come towels
	and wax. 
	A snail spa day.
	
	
	There is no shape
	more entrancing
	than a spiral. 
	Calming\w8
	Soothing\w8
	Hypnotic\w8
	Around and around, infinite depths to trace. 
	Curves sublime. 
	The perfect ratio.
	
	
	Fresh coat of paint
	Brand new accessories
	Washed and waxed
	The dream of every snail
	before hitting the track. 
	What's the point in racing
	if your shell
	doesn't draw
	every eye in the crowd?
	
	
	Day in
	Day out
	Never missing a beat. 
	Practice may not make
	Perfect
	But it does make
	Better
	than the competition.
	
	
	Finally
	the moment has come. 
	Picked from the crowd
	Chosen above the rest
	At long last
	Sponsored. 
	I'll make my mark on the leaderboards
	On racing culture
	And in poetry, too. 
	You won't regret
	your choice.
	">>
	_poems = ProcessPoems(_poems,0,"\b[12]","\f[name,Courier New]")
	parallel _poems
}

