Poetry.Concrete : sequential
{
	_poems = <<"
    ::               the unmistakable       curl      of   
    ::           a snail's spiral shell is    to     be    
    ::        admired, for in it you can see   all the     
    ::      mysteries            of life. twisting round   
    ::    and round,  curling in   upon itself, beautiful  
    ::    and free.  a true marvel,  repeating endlessly,  
    ::    yet each  is      unique.  sharing traits, while 
    ::    standing   on      their   own, wholly complete. 
    ::    strength,        beauty,   perfectly woven       
    ::     together into a dance   that mesmerizes,        
    ::      leaving onlookers    entranced by its          
    ::         allure.        many have wondered           
    ::   where the       power of these structures         
    :: originates, captivated by their pull. the           
    ::  truth? a shell simply reflects the                 
    ::          universe       itself.                     
	
	
	::                         flight.             
	::                    the flutter              
	::                of feathers as the powerful  
	::           beat of wings    propels me       
	::        swiftly towards   my goal. eyes      
	::       are drawn to    these elegant         
	::       appendages,   in awe of their avian   
	::        splendor, an  envy unmatched by even 
	::         the greatest mechanical marvels.    
	::          a simple   beauty that can         
	::          only be  found amongst the sky,    
	::          a gift  from     the heavens.      
	::       style    and  grace unparalleled,     
	::  speed unrivaled,  the open skies           
	:: are the ultimate  racetrack.                
	::  no limits, no obstacles,                   
	::  the purest expression                      
	::    of our art.                              
	
	
	::                                             the   
	::                                            humble 
	::                                          worm can 
	::                                         teach  us 
	::                                       many things 
	::                                      as we watch  
	::                                     it crawl by.  
	::         squiggling,                squirming,     
	::       wholly content              to live its     
	::     simple life, unaffected by the pressures      
	::   of snail society. a peaceful existence,         
	::  small and fragile, but with purpose and          
	:: virtue. who can say they are better               
	:: than a being      whose happiness                 
	:: is only ever                                      
	::  threatened                                       
	::   by birds?                                       
	
	
	::                                 smells    
	::                               of grease   
	::                              and oil      
	::                             fill the      
	::                           air. a clank as 
	::                         a bolt is set on  
	::                      the bench. rusted,   
	::                   in need of              
	::                replacement.               
	::    shiny     new parts                    
	::  are pulled from the                      
	:: shelf. score! i'm                         
	::        getting                            
	::      the real                             
	::  good stuff                               
	::    today!                                 
	
	
	::               the shade from the               
	::          branches of an old oak tree           
	::        shouldn't be taken for granted.         
	::      a tree   so large and      generous       
	::   takes many     years to grow,   and ideal    
	::  placement   requires thought   and    care.   
	:: take this  time to thank those who came before 
	::  for the comforts you now enjoy, and pass it   
	::   forward by leaving a similarly thoughtful    
	::          legacy for the next generation        
	::                who comes after.                
	::                  while they                    
	::                   may   not                    
	::                   remember                     
	::                   your name,                   
	::                  you will have                 
	::               left a tangible mark             
	::             of good  upon the  world.          
	
	
	::                                     dark glasses. 
	::    is there anything cooler      than a    simple 
	:: pair of  shades?    blacked out lenses,    and a  
	::  stylish new     shape will     impress  all who  
	::     look on      from the         side, wishing   
	::       they    could have           eyewear so     
	::         slick. the envy              of all,      
	::            unmatched                   in         
	::              flair.                               
	
	
	::                                      we all 
	::                                    have our 
	::                        own      obstacles   
	::                        to    overcome in    
	::                      life. very often,      
	::                      they come in a         
	::                     physical form           
	::                  which blocks               
	::               our paths. but                
	::            fear not, many                   
	::          a snail   has                      
	::       been faced with                       
	::     a large stick                           
	::  and found the                              
	:: courage   to                                
	:: overcome it                                 
	::  and go on.                                 
	
	
	::                                     they     seem 
	::                                       so     sad, 
	::                                        on   the   
	::                         sidelines all  the time.  
	::                      marginalized,  or  at worst  
	::                 forgotten entirely. surely there  
	::            is a place for            them amongst 
	::       us? perhaps snails are not the only ones    
	::   who are fit to race? it seems a shame to so     
	:: harshly exclude our fellow mollusks this way.     
	
	
	::           around and around it goes,         
	::        an unending loop of competition       
	::      and fame.  excitement, improvement,     
	::    sportsmanship, teamwork. throngs gather   
	::   to witness                     as we take  
	::  these turns                      again and  
	:: again and                          again and 
	:: again,                                always 
	:: the same                             and yet 
	:: new every                            time. a 
	::  thrill you                       can't find 
	::   anywhere but                   the  track. 
	::    nothing compares to the moment we begin.  
	::      the anticipation of the crowd, the      
	::         feel of freshly groomed dirt         
	::             underneath your foot.            
	
	
	::                          the radio   
	::                 makes me feel alive. 
	::            the weather, the news, or 
	::            those doo-wop tunes. it's 
	::            all good to       me,  so 
	::            pick      a station   and 
	::            crank  it             up! 
	::            do                    do, 
	::            da                    da, 
	::           dum                    dum 
	::           da,                     do 
	::           be              do! do you 
	::   see? i could         train all day 
	::  long! nothing        could keep  me 
	:: from  reaching        my  potential. 
	:: just keep that        radio playing, 
	::  and i'll  be            the best    
	::   snail ever.                        
	
	
	::                         crisp,        
	::                   cool leaves are     
	::                a treat, one to be     
	::              cherished  and admired.  
	::             a  single  leaf can feed  
	::            a  snail  well for a day.  
	::           a head?  feast for family   
	::         and friends.   let us all     
	::        be  thankful for  the day      
	::      our ancestors befriended         
	::     this  species of farmers          
	::     who provide for us with           
	::     leaves aplenty, food              
	::     for  all,  shared                 
	::    so   generously.                   
	::   thanks                              
	::  for the                              
	:: greens!                               
	
	
	::                                    a warm breeze  
	::                        takes the sting out of the 
	::                  air. winter's last grip finally  
	::               releasing as buds begin to sprout.  
	::            the world comes out of  its slumber,   
	::          everything buzzing,  alive.   a long     
	::         hibernation  finally   ended, it all      
	::        begins  anew.      a       cycle as        
	::       old as  time     itself, going back         
	::       for eons.     it       encompasses          
	::      more  than   just the weather; all           
	::      life follows  similar patterns if            
	::      you    look            closely.              
	::      indeed,  from the tiniest of                 
	::      atoms to       the largest                   
	::    of  galaxies, the very                         
	::  same       principles                            
	:: apply.                                            
	
	
	::         ribbit.                     a giant          
	::      leap into the               mud. a  plop        
	::      as   drops fly              up into   the       
	::     air,  then  fall           back down    and      
	::     rain  upon  those       nearby. splat. that      
	::       is  how  to tell a frog is near, it  will      
	::      always   be given away by noise,  whether       
	::      it's   croaking or jumping or one      of       
	::     the many other strange behaviors that frogs      
	::    exhibit. though  they may be unusual, they are    
	::   to be respected    and feared,  for they seem to   
	:: be unhindered by fears of their own. many a tale has 
	:: been  told of snails             entering a   frog's 
	::  mouth,           but you'll find           none of  
	::   a successful escape. the all-consumer, the great   
	::    hunger. were they bigger, they might even be      
	::         apex predators, rivaling humanity.           
	
	
	::                     delicate                       
	::     stems push    towards the                      
	::   sky, unfurling their petals                      
	::  and revealing the colors that                     
	:: wait inside. splashes of vivid                     
	:: hue, drops         of heaven                       
	::   dotted    across   the grass.                    
	::   these   petals  in   a myriad                    
	::     of   styles bring  simple joy                  
	::  to all  who observe  their beauty.                
	:: reds and   purples,  pinks and vivid               
	:: yellows. a          symphony of a                  
	:: thousand different shades, waving                  
	:: in the breeze, beckoning to bees                   
	::  and other pollinators. their           dance is   
	::    known to captivate; after all, it is their sole 
	::            purpose in   life. a mission which they 
	::              perform       very well indeed.       
	
	
	::                                      a symbol,    
	::                             powerful and freeing. 
	::                        beauty and grace, power and
	::                    speed, light and    delicate.  
	::               tiny, intricate   details woven     
	::             into a simple   but memorable         
	::           shape. after   you've seen one          
	::          you'll feel   their allure,              
	::     as  we all do.  a longing for                 
	::    the freedom    of the skies,                   
	::   the grace   and elegance of                     
	::   birds,    the chance to                         
	::  soar.   alas, it is not                          
	::   for  us. a feather                              
	::   is merely                                       
	::   a dream that                                    
	:: can't                                             
	:: be.                                               
	
	
	::                   luck.                
	::              it's fickle,              
	::            isn't it?  one   moment     
	::           everything goes your way,    
	::            the next everything falls   
	::              apart, leaving you alone  
	::         on the racetrack, humbled. and 
	::        as smoke pours from your shell, 
	::       you can't help but ask yourself  
	::        "why?"  you did everything      
	::         right, followed all safety     
	::          rules and recommendations,    
	::           and yet it all blew up.      
	::                but   that's            
	::              the      risk             
	::           we all                       
	::       take in                          
	:: this game.                             
	
	
	::                                             pop   
	::                                   pop      pop,   
	::                 pop,   hiss,     pop  pop, hiss,  
	::                  pop, fwoosh,   pop    pop  pop.  
	::                  the  sounds of  a   cozy    fire,
	::                  or the sounds of   your     hard 
	::                   work going up in  flames on the 
	::                   track. perhaps it is wise  to   
	::                 follow the safety warnings when   
	::              using powerful equipment. but then,  
	::       sometimes the risks  are worth   it for the 
	::     rewards.     a healthy    risk  can turn the  
	::  tide of a  race and put you far in the  lead, on 
	:: pace to   easily break world records.  but if it  
	:: goes wrong... pop pop, hiss, crackle, pop.        
	
	
	::                            way up                  
	::                      high above us,                
	::                keeping moisture out of             
	::               our reach. a cruel way to            
	::           taunt    us, making us beg for           
	::          the   water we need for basic life.       
	::       then  again, they also provide     much      
	::      needed  protection  from the sun's   harsh    
	::    rays, so perhaps  they are not all bad.   some  
	::  say they can also serve as omens, with some shapes
	:: bringing good luck, like snails and engines. still 
	::  others say they   are simply pretty   to look at. 
	
	
	::          a           
	::         far          
	::        sound,        
	::       perhaps        
	::      dripping?       
	::     a splash, a      
	::    pitter-patter,    
	::   the  sounds of a   
	::  leak   or a faucet  
	:: left  open. droplets 
	:: fall  onto the floor.
	:: that  will be soaked 
	:: come  morning if not 
	:: attended to. but in  
	::  the middle of the   
	::   night, who will    
	::     be awake to      
	::       notice?        
	
	
	::        at long                                   
	::    last, it's the                                
	::   day of the race!                               
	::  go and get a helium                             
	:: toy  to carry, don't                             
	:: let  it go! maybe tie                            
	:: it   to your wrist so                            
	:: it   doesn't fly away.                           
	:: oh   no—there it goes!                           
	::  you'll need a strong                            
	::    grip next time, a                             
	::      balloon always                              
	::         desires to fly                           
	::                high              up into the     
	::               sky,            far          away  
	::               from        where               you
	::                can     even                      
	::                  see it.                         
	">>
	
	_poems = ProcessPoems(_poems,0,"\b[2]","\f[height,-4]","\f[name,courier new]")
	// _poems = REPLACE(_poems,C_CRLF,"\n")
	// _poems = REPLACE(_poems,"\n::","\n ")
	// _poems = "\![no-autopause]\1\b[2]\_q\f[name,courier new]\f[height,-4]\f[align,left]" + _poems
	_poems = SkipSpaces(_poems)
	parallel _poems
}